# Git commit author

When creating commits in this repo:

- Author name: `theworker02`
- Author email: `theworker02@users.noreply.github.com`
- Prefer the repo-local git config (`user.name` / `user.email`). Do not change `--global`.
- If you must override identity on the CLI:

```bash
git -c user.name="theworker02" -c user.email="theworker02@users.noreply.github.com" commit ...
```

- Never use `CursorAgent`, `Cursor`, or any other Cursor-default identity as commit author.
- Do not rewrite existing commit history to change authors unless the user explicitly asks.
